doc:sch-1-sec-26wf-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "26WF(3) Exception—remedial action" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) If:  (a) a loss of information is covered by paragraph 26WE(2)(b); and  (b) the APP entity, credit reporting body, credit provider or file number recipient, as the case may be, takes action in relation to the loss; and  (c) the APP entity, credit reporting body, credit provider or file number recipient, as the case may be, does so before there is unauthorised access to, or unauthorised disclosure of, the information; and  (d) as a result of the action, there is no unauthorised access to, or unauthorised disclosure of, the information; the loss is not, and is taken never to have been:  (e) an eligible data breach of the APP entity, credit reporting body, credit provider or file number recipient, as the case may be; or  (f) an eligible data breach of any other entity." ;
    cof:pageNumber "11"^^xsd:integer .

concept:privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017-sch-1-sec-26wf-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "26WF(4) Exception—remedial action"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-26wf-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) If:  (a) a loss of information is covered by paragraph 26WE(2)(b); and  (b) the APP entity, credit reporting body, credit provider or file number recipient, as the case may be, takes action in relation to the loss; and  (c) the APP entity, credit reporting body, credit provider or file number recipient, as the case may be, does so:  Amendments  Schedule 1  No. 12, 2017 Privacy Amendment (Notifiable Data Breaches) Act 2017  (i) after there is unauthorised access to, or unauthorised disclosure of, the information; and  (ii) before the access or disclosure results in serious harm to any of the individuals to whom the information relates; and  (d) as a result of the action, a reasonable person would conclude that the access or disclosure would not be likely to result in serious harm to any of those individuals; the loss is not, and is taken never to have been:  (e) an eligible data breach of the APP entity, credit reporting body, credit provider or file number recipient, as the case may be; or  (f) an eligible data breach of any other entity." ;
    skos:definition "(4) If:  (a) a loss of information is covered by paragraph 26WE(2)(b); and  (b) the APP entity, credit reporting body, credit provider or file number recipient, as the case may be, takes action in relation to the loss; and  (c) the APP entity, credit reporting body, credit provider or file number recipient, as the case may be, does so:  Amendments  Schedule 1  No. 12, 2017 Privacy Amendment (Notifiable Data Breaches) Act 2017  (i) after there is unauthorised access to, or unauthorised disclosure of, the information; and  (ii) before the access or disclosure results in serious harm to any of the individuals to whom the information relates; and  (d) as a result of the action, a reasonable person would conclude that the access or disclosure would not be likely to result in serious harm to any of those individuals; the loss is not, and is taken never to have been:  (e) an eligible data breach of the APP entity, credit reporting body, credit provider or file number recipient, as the case may be; or  (f) an eligible data breach of any other entity."@en ;
