doc:sch-1-sec-26wf-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "26WF(4) Exception—remedial action" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) If:  (a) a loss of information is covered by paragraph 26WE(2)(b); and  (b) the APP entity, credit reporting body, credit provider or file number recipient, as the case may be, takes action in relation to the loss; and  (c) the APP entity, credit reporting body, credit provider or file number recipient, as the case may be, does so:  Amendments  Schedule 1  No. 12, 2017 Privacy Amendment (Notifiable Data Breaches) Act 2017  (i) after there is unauthorised access to, or unauthorised disclosure of, the information; and  (ii) before the access or disclosure results in serious harm to any of the individuals to whom the information relates; and  (d) as a result of the action, a reasonable person would conclude that the access or disclosure would not be likely to result in serious harm to any of those individuals; the loss is not, and is taken never to have been:  (e) an eligible data breach of the APP entity, credit reporting body, credit provider or file number recipient, as the case may be; or  (f) an eligible data breach of any other entity." ;
    cof:pageNumber "11"^^xsd:integer .

concept:privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017-sch-1-sec-26wf-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "26WF(5) Exception—remedial action"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-26wf-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) If:  (a) a loss of information is covered by paragraph 26WE(2)(b); and  (b) the APP entity, credit reporting body, credit provider or file number recipient, as the case may be, takes action in relation to the loss; and  (c) the APP entity, credit reporting body, credit provider or file number recipient, as the case may be, does so:  (i) after there is unauthorised access to, or unauthorised disclosure of, the information; and  (ii) before the access or disclosure results in serious harm to a particular individual to whom the information relates; and  (d) as a result of the action, a reasonable person would conclude that the access or disclosure would not be likely to result in serious harm to the individual; this Part does not require:  (e) the APP entity, credit reporting body, credit provider or file number recipient, as the case may be; or  (f) any other entity; to take steps to notify the individual of the contents of a statement that relates to the loss.  Schedule 1  Amendments  Privacy Amendment (Notifiable Data Breaches) Act 2017 No. 12, 2017" ;
    skos:definition "(5) If:  (a) a loss of information is covered by paragraph 26WE(2)(b); and  (b) the APP entity, credit reporting body, credit provider or file number recipient, as the case may be, takes action in relation to the loss; and  (c) the APP entity, credit reporting body, credit provider or file number recipient, as the case may be, does so:  (i) after there is unauthorised access to, or unauthorised disclosure of, the information; and  (ii) before the access or disclosure results in serious harm to a particular individual to whom the information relates; and  (d) as a result of the action, a reasonable person would conclude that the access or disclosure would not be likely to result in serious harm to the individual; this Part does not require:  (e) the APP entity, credit reporting body, credit provider or file number recipient, as the case may be; or  (f) any other entity; to take steps to notify the individual of the contents of a statement that relates to the loss.  Schedule 1  Amendments  Privacy Amendment (Notifiable Data Breaches) Act 2017 No. 12, 2017"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "22303fd16e2c1938293974cbeed61209587faf25d88e6772af10020758be4fe7" ;
    values:partOf concept:privacy-amendment-notifiable-data-breaches-act-2017-sch-1-sec-26wf ;
    cof:pageNumber "11"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Exemption from notification requirement for certain entities taking action in relation to loss of information." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
